    "description": "ExteNet develops and operates outdoor and in-building wireless infrastructure, fiber networks, and related connectivity systems for mobile carriers, venue owners, and enterprise customers. The company follows an asset-heavy model built around long-lived communications infrastructure and recurring carrier or venue revenues rather than retail service revenues. Public materials describe ExteNet as the largest privately held U.S. provider focused on DAS, small cells, fiber, and other advanced connectivity solutions. Its footprint is national, and the company relocated its headquarters to Frisco, Texas while continuing to serve carrier and enterprise customers across major U.S. markets. John Hancock led the acquisition of an approximately 30% stake in 2020, and ExteNet announced the closing of the Manulife-led investment in 2021 alongside existing owners Digital Colony and Stonepeak. Manulife's infrastructure team identifies the investment with Fund II.",
